<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Leonard calls in the morning and is seen the same day. Last night he refereed a full card of eight bouts in an arena without air conditioning during a heat wave, sweating through two shirts, and drank little because he did not want to leave the ring between bouts. He ate a late supper and took his losartan-hydrochlorothiazide tablet this morning as usual. Since getting up he has felt lightheaded and his vision has grayed when he stands quickly, easing when he sits; he has not fainted. He is thirsty, has passed little dark urine, and has cramps in his calves. He has had no chest discomfort, palpitations, breathlessness, vomiting or diarrhea. He did not hold his tablet because he did not feel ill when he took it. His home readings over the past week, in the heat, were about 118/74 mmHg. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>This morning, after refereeing a full card in a heat wave last night</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Vision grays on standing; no fainting</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Heavy sweating, little to drink, and losartan 100 mg with hydrochlorothiazide 25 mg taken this morning</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Thirst, dark urine, calf cramps; no chest pain, palpitations, breathlessness, vomiting or diarrhea</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Better sitting or lying</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

