    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Volume depletion on a thiazide in summer heat (E86.0)</content>. Orthostatic hypotension from salt and water loss in heavy sweating, made worse by the thiazide and the angiotensin receptor blocker: creatinine 1.44 mg/dL against 1.06 three weeks ago, urea nitrogen 32 mg/dL, sodium 133 and potassium 3.3 mmol/L. The ECG shows sinus tachycardia with no ischemia or arrhythmia. He can drink, is not vomiting and is not confused, so oral rehydration at home is safe. The basic metabolic panel planned two weeks after the dose increase was not drawn, so this is the first check since then. [S]<list><item>Hold losartan-hydrochlorothiazide until the recheck in one week; check home blood pressure twice a day and call for readings above 160/100 mmHg.</item><item>Drink two to three liters today, including salted broth and an oral rehydration drink, then enough to keep the urine pale; potassium-rich foods (bananas, potatoes, tomatoes).</item><item>No refereeing until the recheck.</item><item>Repeat basic metabolic panel and blood pressure at next week&apos;s preventive visit, which becomes the recheck.</item><item>Emergency care for fainting, chest pain, palpitations or confusion.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Hypertensive heart disease (I11.9)</content>. Blood pressure is low today from volume loss; the regimen will be reviewed at the recheck, since a thiazide is a poor fit for a man who sweats heavily at work in the heat, as the cardiologist foresaw. [S]<list><item>Continue atorvastatin.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults (2025)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Recheck at the preventive visit in one week, or sooner for the warning signs above. Next scheduled visit 1946-07-28: periodic adult preventive visit and recheck after the sick visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

